==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hwō}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|hū}}, {{cog|osx|hū}} ({{cog|nl|hoe}}), {{cog|goh|wuo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|hū}}

===Adverb===
{{ang-adv|hū}}

# [[how|How]], in all senses, including:
## To [[what]] [[degree]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' eald is þīn dohtor?|'''How''' old is your daughter?}}
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' miċel fēos hæfst þū mid þē?|'''How''' much money do you have with you?}}
## In [[what]] [[manner]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' sæġþ man þæt on Englisċ?|'''How''' do you say that in English?}}
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' færst þū?|'''How''' are you? (Literally: "'''How''' are you faring?")}}
## In [[what]] [[state]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' wæs þīn dæġ?|'''How''' was your day?}}
##: {{ux|ang|Þū canst Ælfrēd cyning? '''Hū''' is hē?|You know King Alfred? '''What''' is he '''like'''?}}
## ''Used in exclamations''
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' hleahtorlīċ!|'''How''' ridiculous!}}
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' gōd hund!|'''What''' a good dog!}}

===Conjunction===
{{ang-con|head=hū}}

# [[how|How]], in all senses:
## In [[what]] [[manner]]
##: {{ux|ang|Iċ leornode '''hū''' man wæġn ġebētt.|I learned '''how''' to repair a wagon.}}
##: {{ux|ang|Hīe āxodon '''hū''' hīe helpan meahten.|They asked '''how''' they could help.}}
## [[that|That]], the fact that ''(introducing direct statements)''
##: {{ux|ang|Iċ him sæġde '''hū''' iċ wǣre æt hām ealne dæġ and ne ġehīerde nāwiht.|I told them '''how''' I'd been at home all day and hadn't heard a thing.}}
##: {{ux|ang|Þæt is tō wundriġenne '''hū''' hīe þā bryċġe swā hrædlīċe ġefyldon.|It's amazing '''how''' they completed the bridge so quickly.}}

